CVE-2024-34478 # "CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions." This vulnerability is BTC only, BSC does not have the issue.
CVE-2021-43668 # "CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference", the repo: syndtr/goleveldb is not actively maintained, seems there is no fix for this crash yet, BSC used pebbleDB to replaced levelDB, so ignore this vulnerability.
CVE-2025-47908 # "CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption ('Resource Exhaustion')", This vulnerability is only for RPC nodes which have specifically enabled malicous Cors options, which is unlikely to happen.
CVE-2025-64702 # "CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling" in quic-go. Unreachable: quic-go is linked only via prysmaticlabs/prysm -> libp2p, which L2P imports for BLS crypto and validator account helpers. No libp2p host is ever created and QUIC/HTTP3 is not used by the devp2p stack. Upgrading is blocked by libp2p v0.38.1, which is pinned by prysm v5.3.2 and does not compile against quic-go >= v0.60.
CVE-2026-40898 # "CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling" in quic-go (HTTP/3 trailers). Same reachability and upgrade constraints as CVE-2025-64702.
CVE-2026-21434 # "CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling" in webtransport-go. Unreachable: WebTransport is only reachable through libp2p, which L2P never instantiates. Upgrade blocked by the same libp2p/prysm pin.
CVE-2026-21435 # "CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption" in webtransport-go. Same reachability and upgrade constraints as CVE-2026-21434.
CVE-2026-21438 # "CWE-401: Memory Leak" in webtransport-go. Same reachability and upgrade constraints as CVE-2026-21434.
CVE-2026-57497 # "CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling" in webtransport-go. Same reachability and upgrade constraints as CVE-2026-21434.
CVE-2026-54908 # "CWE-125: Out-of-bounds Read" in pion/dtls, reachable only through a DTLS handshake. L2P never opens a DTLS connection; the module is linked in as a transitive dependency of pion/stun and libp2p. No fixed release exists for the v2 module line.
CVE-2026-26014 # "CWE-200: Information Exposure" in pion/dtls (AES-GCM nonce reuse). Same reachability as CVE-2026-54908; requires an established DTLS session, which L2P never creates.
CVE-2026-54909 # "CWE-20: Improper Input Validation" (panic in XORMappedAddress.GetFromAs) in pion/stun. L2P's own STUN client in p2p/nat/stun.go was migrated to github.com/pion/stun/v3 v3.1.7, which contains the fix. The finding that remains applies to the unfixed pion/stun v0.6.1 that libp2p pulls in transitively via prysm; that code path is never executed because L2P never creates a libp2p host.
